// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 12 (Impl-Q): the push_ptr pointee retention
// fix (closing Impl-J's Wave-8 flag — escape_ref_outer_ok.sn deferred the
// runtime retain to this tier with "the pushed target 'y' is never read
// after the push"). A `ref<int>` of a local is a stack-slot address, not
// an object header: pushing it into a `list<ref<int>>` must retain the
// POINTEE (for a scalar target, nothing — the borrow discipline owns the
// target's lifetime), never the slot. The round trip: the local's value
// is UNCHANGED by the push (the old blind sn_retain treated the slot as
// an Obj header and clobbered 99 -> 100), and the list read gives the
// right pointee. Both push spellings: the named ref and the inline
// address().
//
// Run-OK golden case (tests/golden.rs).

fn main() {
    int x = 99
    list<ref<int>> box = []
    ref<int> r = address(x)
    box.push(r)
    print(x)
    print(value(box[0]))
    box.push(address(x))
    print(x)
    print(value(box[1]))
}
